.TH PURA 1 "October 2026" "pura 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pura \- safe Linux disk space recovery utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pura
.RB [ \,\-n|\-\-dry-run\, ]
.RB [ \,\-y|\-\-yes\, ]
.RB [ \,\-\-aggressive\, ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pura
cleans rebuildable user caches, distribution package caches, old systemd journal entries, managed temporary files, and the current user's trash. It is a POSIX sh executable and is independent of the calling shell.
.PP
The default mode is deliberately conservative. It never formats a device, removes a partition table, writes to a raw block device, runs dd/wipefs/mkfs, removes documents, or runs autoremove or Docker prune.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan [PATH]
Read-only filesystem and first-level directory usage report. Defaults to /.
.TP
.B scan disk /dev/sdX
Show block-device filesystem and mounted paths, without changing anything.
.TP
.B clean all
Run the safe cache, package-cache, journal, temp, and trash plan.
.TP
.B clean caches
Clean known rebuildable caches below the current user's cache directory.
.TP
.B clean packages
Clean the detected package-manager cache without removing installed packages.
.TP
.B clean logs
Vacuum systemd journal entries older than 14 days.
.TP
.B clean temp
Run systemd-tmpfiles --clean when available.
.TP
.B clean trash
Empty the current user's trash permanently.
.TP
.B clean /dev/sdX
Find mounted filesystems on the device and clean only current-user cache/trash paths located on those filesystems. Requires typing CLEAN /dev/sdX. No raw device writes occur.
.TP
.B clean disk /dev/sdX
Equivalent explicit form of clean /dev/sdX.
.TP
.B doctor
Show detected distribution and optional tools.
.TP
.B explain
Print the safety boundaries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -n , --dry-run
Print the plan without making changes.
.TP
.BR -y , --yes
Skip normal safe-clean confirmation. It does not bypass the typed confirmation for device cleanup.
.TP
.B --aggressive
Clear additional contents of the current user's cache root and remove unused Flatpak runtimes.
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Show help.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pura scan
pura clean all --dry-run
sudo pura clean packages
pura clean /dev/sda
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache
User cache root, constrained by XDG_CACHE_HOME when set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash
Current user's trash.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The requested operation completed or was safely skipped.
.TP
1
Invalid input, unsafe or unavailable target, or command failure.
